    "field": "Arctic climate change",
    "problem": "Previous climate projections potentially underestimate the rate and magnitude of increasing Arctic precipitation, with newer models revealing that the transition to a rain-dominated climate will occur faster and be larger than previously anticipated.",
    "method": "The authors analyze and compare Arctic precipitation, snowfall, and rainfall outputs from CMIP6 and CMIP5 climate model ensembles under high-emission scenarios, validating historical simulations against ERA5 and GPCP observational datasets to project future changes in the hydrological cycle.",
    "task": "The task is to compare Arctic precipitation projections from CMIP6 and CMIP5 climate models to evaluate how new models project faster and larger increases in rainfall and an earlier transition from a snow- to a rain-dominated regime than previously anticipated.",
